---
const tooling = [
  "React",
  "TypeScript",
  "JavaScript",
  "Capacitor",
  "SCSS",
  "Styled Components",
  "Jest",
  "Cypress",
  "Node.js",
  "Express",
  "MongoDB",
  "OpenLayers",
  "Git",
  "Github Copilot",
  "Python",
  "PostgreSQL",
  "Supabase",
]
---

<article class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-8 text-slate-300 md:flex-row">
  <div
    class="order-2 text-pretty [&>p]:mb-4 [&>p>a]:underline-offset-4 [&>p>a]:transition-colors [&>p>a]:hover:text-[rgb(var(--color-accent))] [&>p>a>strong]:font-mono [&>p>a>strong]:font-normal [&>p>a>strong]:text-[rgb(var(--color-accent))] md:order-1"
  >
    <p>
      I'm Jaime, a software engineer from Zaragoza with a background in graphic design. That mix of design sensitivity and engineering discipline still shapes the way I build products: clean interfaces, strong visual polish, and code that stays maintainable as projects grow.
    </p>

    <p>
      I've worked in a <a href="https://garvira.com/" target="_blank"><strong>digital services cooperative</strong></a>, a <a href="https://cleverpy.com/" target="_blank"><strong>product-focused start-up</strong></a>, and currently at <a href="https://www.capgemini.com/es-es/" target="_blank"><strong>Capgemini</strong></a>, contributing to frontend solutions for different clients and business contexts.
    </p>

    <p class="[&>strong]:font-mono [&>strong]:font-normal [&>strong]:font-bold [&>strong]:text-[rgb(var(--color-accent))]">
      I enjoy building <strong>clear</strong>, <strong>reliable</strong>, and <strong>well-crafted</strong> applications, especially when the work involves turning complex requirements into interfaces that feel simple to use.
    </p>

    <p>
      Technologies I use most often:
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,_minmax(150px,_1fr))] gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
      {tooling.map((tool) => (
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-[rgb(var(--color-accent))]">&gt;</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-[rgb(var(--color-text-muted))]">{tool}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
